# L §8.1 (2.1-F12): "A read `of q` and an order term over it ... are each known where every possible label gives it one
# value ... a part whose every possible label is q's is read as q's", at a place that keeps pairs too.  b1 holds
# Ania's batches jb[g1] (9) and jb[g2] (6); its order rank_b[k.batch] is a hole per batch, so the sale of 5 is
# undecided and b1 keeps one hole part of 10 (scratch/exp_r3.py) whose possible labels are (ania, jb[g1]) and (ania,
# jb[g2]).  q1: of ania it is 10, and the sale's cash arrives at b1c as Ania's (1 000.00, carried through); of jb[g1]
# it is a hole.  q2: the leg read of Ania is 5; of each batch a hole.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-15
  start 2021-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source src "test"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
kind funds: unit
kind couples: parties
kind persons: parties
kind gifts: event certain
  leg units: funds
  attr donee: key persons
kind buys: event certain
  leg units: funds
  leg cash: DUK
kind sales: event certain
  leg units: funds
  leg cash: DUK
kind cash_accounts: place one min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(DUK)
  takes k for w order rank[k.owner]
kind lots: holdings
  owned by arrive
  batched
  step 0.0001
  takes k for w order rank_b[k.batch]
place b1: lots idx lives 2021-01-01..
place b1c: cash_accounts DUK lives 2021-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2000-01-01..
place market: outside lives 2000-01-01..
input jb: observed
def rank[p in parties]: int = ?"which money leaves first?" at reader
def rank_b[b in gifts]: int = ?"which lot leaves first?" at reader
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule community = (if p == ania_tomek then 1 else 0)
  rule gifted beats community = (if p == m.donee then 1 else 0) when m in gifts
  rule sold beats community = m.units.amount of p / m.units.amount when m in sales

ask q1: bal(b1, 2025-12-31) of ania, bal(b1c, 2025-12-31) of ania, bal(b1, 2025-12-31) of jb[g1]
ask q2: s.units.amount of ania, s.units.amount of jb[g1], s.units.amount of jb[g2] for s in sales over 2025-03-01..2025-03-01

version cast
  cite src
  known 2021-01-01
  funds + [idx] lives 2018-01-01..
  persons + [ania] lives 1991-03-14..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1989-07-02..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2016-09-10..

version open
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2021-01-01
  opening[b1] = 0 at 2021-01-01 start
  opening[b1c] = 0 at 2021-01-01 start

version j
  cite src
  governs 2025-01..2025-12
  known 2025-01-01
  covers b1, b1c
  jb[g1] = (on: 2025-02-01, kind: gifts, leg units from world to b1 amount 9 idx, donee: ania) "g1"
  jb[g2] = (on: 2025-02-05, kind: gifts, leg units from world to b1 amount 6 idx, donee: ania) "g2"
  jb[s1] = (on: 2025-03-01, kind: sales, leg units from b1 to market amount 5 idx, leg cash from market to b1c amount 1000.00 DUK) "s1"
=== expect
q1: (10 idx, 1 000.00 DUK, ?"b1: 10 idx may be jb[g1]'s: which lot leaves first?" (b1))
...
q2 (s = jb[s1]): (5 idx, ?"b1: 5 idx may be jb[g1]'s: which lot leaves first?" (b1), ?"b1: 5 idx may be jb[g2]'s: which lot leaves first?" (b1))
...
